ste my best weapon (♠2). If the landlord beats it, they’ll have to use a high card, reducing their options later. If they pass, my teammate might get a chance to play.  \n\nI’ll rule out the pair of 4s because playing two cards now reduces my hand size but leaves me with weaker singles, and the landlord could have a pair to beat it easily (with many high pairs still unknown). I’ll also rule out the very low singles (4, 6, 10) because they give the landlord an easy pass or cheap win. ♥K is a reasonable balance—not too low, not my best.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": ["♥K"]}'}
